From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TG5050 reconstruction <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: sunxi: stop DSI output before panel and clock teardown

The DSI atomic-disable path previously unprepared the panel, powered off
the PHY and clocks, and only then disabled DSI output and exited TCON mode.
That leaves output registers and interrupt state to be changed after the
hardware required to perform the shutdown has already been reset.

Stop the DSI output and exit TCON mode while the link is still powered, then
put the panel to sleep and complete PHY/clock/reset teardown. This is the
common disable sequence used by output removal, suspend, and shutdown.

--- a/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/drm/sunxi_drm_dsi.c
@@ -938,6 +938,9 @@
 #endif
 	if (dsi->te_gpio)
 		esd_watchdog_stop(dsi->esd_wdt);
+	sunxi_dsi_disable_output(dsi);
+	sunxi_tcon_mode_exit(dsi->sdrm.tcon_dev);
+
 	drm_panel_disable(dsi->sdrm.panel);
 
 	drm_panel_unprepare(dsi->sdrm.panel);
@@ -958,9 +961,6 @@
 	sunxi_lcd_pin_set_state(dsi->dev, "sleep");
 	if (dsi->slave)
 		sunxi_lcd_pin_set_state(dsi->slave->dev, "sleep");
-	sunxi_dsi_disable_output(dsi);
-	sunxi_tcon_mode_exit(dsi->sdrm.tcon_dev);
-
 	dsi->enable = false;
 	DRM_DEBUG_DRIVER("%s finish\n", __FUNCTION__);
 }
